uestion/worked-solution "The zeros of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x$ are given by\n\n$$\nx=n\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\nTo find the zeros of $f(x)=2\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x-\\frac{\\pi }{6}),$ we replace the $x$ on the left-hand side of the above with $(2x-\\frac{\\pi }{6}).$ This gives\n\n$$\n2x-\\frac{\\pi }{6}=n\\pi .\n$$\n\nSolving for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-\\frac{\\pi }{6} & =n\\pi  \\\\ 2x & =n\\pi +\\frac{\\pi }{6} \\\\ x & =\\frac{\\pi }{12}+\\frac{n\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the zeros are $x=\\frac{\\pi }{12}+\\frac{n\\pi }{2},$ where $n$ is an integer." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-29556/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fabd8865-cc14-508a-aa81-4ba147f7f8d4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-29556"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-117671/selection/440506d17906b3bb4665b471f7fb3ed0170bb512bf494476717641495901a896" :answer/id #uuid "bc0ab833-15ec-5a78-b98e-b0a5ebc8cd87" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{n\\pi }{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117671/selection/512babc0ae3a4c05f232662ba352a60abbcf8ae49b48ecc1f02c63a8d33be413" :answer/id #uuid "f0b05473-bcc5-54a5-b454-e7bc84e3a9d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{n\\pi }{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117671/selection/1f12e0fcdabe89e21bda1982c6cc2e02714b58ddf639e811ef42fc969659e3d1" :answer/id #uuid "7eaad2bb-6739-5a3b-a0f0-ff63413cf5f5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-\\frac{\\pi }{3}+\\frac{n\\pi }{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117671/selection/4c36aa03ab083a8deefcab1826f0acde1fe5f41a412d80165f01522f29252fa9" :answer/id #uuid "c6fd5faa-3ff6-5d33-80f0-4b28ae9e41a8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\frac{n\\pi }{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117671/selection/75d77e38caf62da260aea33b8145f4df558b419d9a50f5202ec1d64adc1a423e" :answer/id #uuid "fc468c49-1e06-5072-93d6-5eb8051c62ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-\\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\frac{n\\pi }{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117671/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "60ec4258-e789-553b-ba87-3b0438148bab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-117671/selection/512babc0ae3a4c05f232662ba352a60abbcf8ae49b48ecc1f02c63a8d33be413" :answer-field/choices ["q-117671/selection/440506d17906b3bb4665b471f7fb3ed0170bb512bf494476717641495901a896" "q-117671/selection/512babc0ae3a4c05f232662ba352a60abbcf8ae49b48ecc1f02c63a8d33be413" "q-117671/selection/1f12e0fcdabe89e21bda1982c6cc2e02714b58ddf639e811ef42fc969659e3d1" "q-117671/selection/4c36aa03ab083a8deefcab1826f0acde1fe5f41a412d80165f01522f29252fa9" "q-117671/selection/75d77e38caf62da260aea33b8145f4df558b419d9a50f5202ec1d64adc1a423e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-117671" :question/id #uuid "7ac30df1-20ef-5dc8-9420-e3dd6c1ddd9d" :question/math-academy-id "q-117671" :question/problem "Which of the following expressions gives all of the zeros of the function $f(x)=4\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3x+\\pi )?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer." :question/worked-solution "The zeros of $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡x$ are given by \n\n$$\nx=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\nTo find the zeros of $f(x)=4\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3x+\\pi ),$ we replace the $x$ on the left-hand side of the above with $(3x+\\pi ).$ This gives\n\n$$\n3x+\\pi =\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi .\n$$\n\nSolving for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x+\\pi  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi  \\\\ 3x & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi -\\pi  \\\\ 3x & =-\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi  \\\\ x & =-\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{n\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the zeros are $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{n\\pi }{3},$ where $n$ is an integer." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-117671/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fabd8865-cc14-508a-aa81-4ba147f7f8d4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-117671"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-81546/selection/536927037ead95932ede1404ec1849295167a778de0a713e9d7238d17050b073" :answer/id #uuid "712173b1-8a83-54a8-be05-e824d52e6a70" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{n\\pi }{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81546/selection/4f05ad282b747c06b07bebb4871757d853af8abb53bd550981d075e2922a842f" :answer/id #uuid "a034fbd5-1026-518d-a2b3-4510c6e2140b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6n\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81546/selection/7730970f72707b1edf10214b0c74b387481856c80bc3bde1b71f14cbfb3cc736" :answer/id #uuid "415c05d7-539b-5ac9-ab5a-4274f7b8114a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\frac{n\\pi }{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81546/selection/82b4ca1faa5e055642901e2ec5db152d770cb6fb6abbc4592a89acaf20ead45b" :answer/id #uuid "60a631aa-e611-5ae9-a5b0-5366dacb9b82" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}+6n\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81546/selection/972c7957fb8ed799b788d9808f5fa625f7a072d8cc27348ce8a74cfa750d8354" :answer/id #uuid "630459d3-f834-5441-a47b-795f9faf5c18" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{6}+3n\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81546/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a6ab3c17-f018-59d3-a1b9-88b7da567525" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-81546/selection/536927037ead95932ede1404ec1849295167a778de0a713e9d7238d17050b073" :answer-field/choices ["q-81546/selection/536927037ead95932ede1404ec1849295167a778de0a713e9d7238d17050b073" "q-81546/selection/4f05ad282b747c06b07bebb4871757d853af8abb53bd550981d075e2922a842f" "q-81546/selection/7730970f72707b1edf10214b0c74b387481856c80bc3bde1b71f14cbfb3cc736" "q-81546/selection/82b4ca1faa5e055642901e2ec5db152d770cb6fb6abbc4592a89acaf20ead45b" "q-81546/selection/972c7957fb8ed799b788d9808f5fa625f7a072d8cc27348ce8a74cfa750d8354"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-81546" :question/id #uuid "a139c5ef-c768-5c96-ba0a-7b4e6441e50e" :question/math-academy-id "q-81546" :question/problem "Which of the following expressions gives all of the zeros of the function $f(x)=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(6x+\\frac{\\pi }{2})?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer." :question/worked-solution "The zeros of $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡x$ are given by \n\n$$\nx=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\nTo find the zeros of $f(x)=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(6x+\\frac{\\pi }{2}),$ we replace the $x$ on the left-hand side of the above with $(6x+\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$ This gives\n\n$$\n6x+\\frac{\\pi }{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi .\n$$\n\nSolving for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6x+\\frac{\\pi }{2} & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi  \\\\ 6x & =n\\pi  \\\\ x & =\\frac{n\\pi }{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the zeros are $x=\\frac{n\\pi }{6},$ where $n$ is an integer." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-81546/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fabd8865-cc14-508a-aa81-4ba147f7f8d4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-81546"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-81545/selection/d8c2012fd9ebb88e02ce566374a341d570a6687055b53c6d4fc7b4c1f5d683fc" :answer/id #uuid "00a8a0f7-6d80-51c9-aa3f-9b586b80325c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi +4n\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81545/selection/dc88946a7a3099d541a715d341ab1cb529d187d01221fcb975ba382dff3ebc27" :answer/id #uuid "5b126c27-830f-5961-a568-81f28560584a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{8}+4n\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81545/selection/463f031e2bc4db9ed93865bcdb3b9