field/validate]} {:db/id "q-117700" :question/id #uuid "94a88f64-34b6-5bf0-b22d-e438ec352322" :question/math-academy-id "q-117700" :question/problem "Which of the following expressions gives all of the vertical asymptotes of the function  $f(x)=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi x}{3}+\\frac{\\pi }{6})?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer." :question/worked-solution "The asymptotes of $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡x$ are given by the expression\n\n$$\nx=n\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\nTo find the asymptotes of $\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi x}{3}+\\frac{\\pi }{6}),$ we replace the $x$ on the left-hand side of the above with $(\\frac{\\pi x}{3}+\\frac{\\pi }{6}).$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\pi x}{3}+\\frac{\\pi }{6}=n\\pi .\n$$\n\nSolving for $x,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\pi x}{3}+\\frac{\\pi }{6} & =n\\pi  \\\\ \\frac{\\pi x}{3} & =-\\frac{\\pi }{6}+n\\pi  \\\\ \\pi x & =-\\frac{\\pi }{2}+3n\\pi  \\\\ x & =-\\frac{1}{2}+3n.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the expression giving all the vertical asymptotes is $x=-\\frac{1}{2}+3n,$ where $n$ is an integer." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-117700/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8854eaba-96c7-5ea8-a071-7ff7c954f943"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-117700"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-117698/selection/7c39e5203a712802ba387ad678fc7aca2778d6adf076702a2ad7866eb1df4f37" :answer/id #uuid "0dd651f3-7ebf-5ba4-a959-178b97dcc31d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\frac{n\\pi }{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117698/selection/3897f1fe7806340ca021fec3fcdb2b5ea22b1a4f9bd2f59e45459c92547ab632" :answer/id #uuid "48c1651b-0d9d-56de-a79a-341d8e5ee39f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\frac{\\pi }{16}+\\frac{n\\pi }{16}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117698/selection/982333ab225c17b2023b97fc86b1c7ab6f7af3e6ec42cdc9c14