ion/1a009a630db7a897cfd656e7efbf1bdde583eabdd866bc5950da7262feff2d73" "q-117707/selection/883487deadef319e50d1a7edc20321a73d158a5cb60a439dcfa47a13c7624a8b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-117707" :question/id #uuid "717d3db3-4268-5678-8f9b-8e1177d7e4db" :question/math-academy-id "q-117707" :question/problem "What is the domain of the function  $f(x)=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{x}{4}-\\frac{\\pi }{2})?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer." :question/worked-solution "The domain of $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡x$ is given by\n\n$$\nx\\ne n\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\nTo find the domain of $\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{x}{4}-\\frac{\\pi }{2}),$ we replace the $x$ on the left-hand side of the above with $(\\frac{x}{4}-\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{x}{4}-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\ne n\\pi .\n$$\n\nSolving for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{4}-\\frac{\\pi }{2} & \\ne n\\pi  \\\\ \\frac{x}{4} & \\ne \\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi  \\\\ x & =2\\pi +4n\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain of the function is $x\\ne 2\\pi +4n\\pi ,$ where $n$ is an integer." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-117707/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd6703d2-36f6-5665-90e3-f75aea5f663b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-117707"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-41106/selection/752b59ea9ff50636a0571fdf3ffdc42fc3acf5e0e3793b0fee434279827e9db7" :answer/id #uuid "a31d5404-f97e-5c11-836a-00d0ee2afd02" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{9}+\\frac{n\\pi }{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-41106/selection/a71e0013af1e932eb635a4aa6b4de9c15bf956ba41ad80fd119b4a6ee94b2ab2" :answer/id #uuid "791299ed-558f-5a2d-9d85-026b4b0c19ac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{3}+\\frac{n\\pi }{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-41106/selection/82ce22e388141ac9c90d4cef2dde1238576d513ab155ddb5f