$\n\nSolving for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x & \\ne \\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi  \\\\ x & \\ne \\frac{\\pi }{2\\cdot 5}+\\frac{n\\pi }{5} \\\\ x & \\ne \\frac{\\pi }{10}+\\frac{n\\pi }{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain of the function is $x\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{10}+\\frac{n\\pi }{5},$ where $n$ is an integer." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-117708/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd6703d2-36f6-5665-90e3-f75aea5f663b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-117708"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
